<title>GERMANY: GERMANY SEES NO REASON TO REVISE 97 DEFICIT FORECAST.</title>
<headline>GERMANY SEES NO REASON TO REVISE 97 DEFICIT FORECAST.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German Finance Ministry on Tuesday said there was &quot;no reason&quot; to revise its forecast for a budget deficit of 2.9 percent of gross domestic product, denying a BBC report that rising unemployment has pushed official expectations to 3.5 percent, above the limit for European monetary union.</p>
<p>&quot;The government's prognosis was in the annual economic report that came out three weeks ago,&quot; a Finance Ministry spokesman told Reuters. &quot;There is no reason to change the prognosis after three weeks.&quot;</p>
</text>
